sec.p:
The sedimentary heterogeneity effect (the transmitted fraction from layer 1 to layer 
                        
                            
                                n
                        ) can be evaluated using the model described by (1)–(6). As shown in Figure 2, the electromagnetic radiation crosses the first layer and only a fraction of it enters the second layer. The reminder is reflected and can be regarded as a loss. In order to show that the loss assumption is well justified, the power of the transmitted waves in layer two (thick arrow in Figure 2) that resides after multiple reflections in layer 1 (dashed arrow in Figure 2) has been calculated. As it is more than three orders of smaller magnitude it can be ignored [7].
